{{also|вы|Вы|вꙑ|Appendix:Variations of "bi"}}
==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|orv|вꙑ-}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*vy-||out}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*(H)ud}} (Derksen) or {{m|ine-pro|*ūd-}} : {{m|ine-pro|*ūt-}} ({{xlit|ru|Черных}}). In Slavic, the final consonant was dropped.

Cognates include {{cog|en|out}}, {{cog|de|aus||out}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|вы-}}

===Prefix===
{{head|ru|prefix|head=вы́-|cat2=verbal prefixes}} {{qualifier|this prefix almost invariably bears the stress in perfective verbs, but not in imperfective verbs}}

# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[out]], [[out from]] {{gloss|describing an action of moving outside from inside}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[идти́]]|to go}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[вы́йти]]|to go out}}
# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[completion]] or [[fulfillment]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[кури́ть]]|to smoke}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[вы́курить]]|to smoke to the end}}

